.TH OROC-MCP 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.0" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-mcp \- Run a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for agent tooling.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc mcp [options] [<workspace\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for agent tooling. By default this subcommand speaks JSON\-RPC over stdio (stdout is reserved for MCP messages). Use \-\-http to run an HTTP/SSE transport.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-stdio\fR
use stdio transport (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-http\fR
use HTTP/SSE transport
.TP
\fB\-\-host=<host>\fR
HTTP bind host (default: 127.0.0.1)
.TP
\fB\-\-port=<port>\fR
HTTP bind port (default: 0 for ephemeral)
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint=<path>\fR
HTTP endpoint path (default: /mcp; normalizes mcp,/mcp,/mcp/)
.TP
\fB\-\-token=<token>\fR
require bearer token (default: disabled on loopback, auto\-generated otherwise)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auth\fR
disable token auth (loopback only)
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace=<path>\fR
explicit workspace root (default: current directory or <workspace\-dir>)
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
workspace\-relative oro.toml/oro.ini path to use as the active project config
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-workspace\-only\fR
restrict filesystem reads to the workspace root (disables read_file)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-read\-outside\-workspace\fR
allow reading arbitrary files outside the workspace root (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-replace\-sse\-stream\fR
allow a new SSE connection to replace an existing one for the same session id
.SH NOTES
.PP
Stdio mode disables JSON logs and suppresses INFO output so stdout remains valid MCP JSON\-RPC. HTTP mode implements MCP Streamable HTTP (2025\-06\-18); clients must call initialize first and then include Mcp\-Session\-Id on subsequent requests. The server publishes descriptive MCP tool metadata, including standard titles, safety annotations, a custom metadata object, and structured tool results to help human and AI clients choose the right operation without shell parsing. Use the MCP `search_docs` tool for topic\-driven discovery across README, MCP, API, config, and manpage resources before falling back to manual resource walking. When \-\-config is omitted, the active config defaults to oro.toml and falls back to oro.ini when that is the only standard project config present in the workspace. resources/list includes the workspace root and, when present, the active config file, project\-local docs under conventional paths, and installed runtime\-doc:/ references for shipped API, CLI, config, MCP, README, llms.txt, and man1/man3/man7 docs when available. Prefer runtime\-doc:/ resources for runtime behavior and API contracts, and workspace:/ resources for the current app's config and local docs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc mcp \-\-stdio .\fR
start an MCP server over stdio for the current workspace
.TP
\fBoroc mcp \-\-http \-\-host=127.0.0.1 \-\-port=8080 .\fR
expose the MCP server over local HTTP/SSE
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
